;;; hash-short-aliases-dropped.slatl — Motoi Scheme Reference · broken-examples
;;;
;;; A broken-example is kept ON PURPOSE (CLAUDE.md § Broken-examples teach
;;; the differences). `hash-ref` and `hash-set!` were Motoi-substrate short
;;; aliases for `hash-table-ref`/`hash-table-set!`. They were dropped from
;;; Motoi's wired surface on 2026-07-24: they are non-standard divergent names
;;; for SRFI-125 verbs, and the standard is locked to SRFI-125's spellings.
;;;
;;; Provenance for the DECISION: the Priya 2026-07-18 audit found 636 uses of
;;; `hash-ref` in the Motoi corpus, and both names were once installed as CORE
;;; for cross-dialect convenience. Under the locked standard (CLAUDE.md
;;; § standard library) a divergent name that duplicates a standard verb is a
;;; bug, so the short aliases were retired. Verbatim originals archived at
;;; scheme/reference/_archive/32-hash-divergent-blocks-20260724/.

(dialect :applies ("motoi") :note "broken-example — hash-ref / hash-set! are dropped sister-dialect short aliases")

(broken-example :name "hash-ref"
  :library "broken-examples"
  :teaches "no-short-aliases-for-standard-hash-verbs"
  :std-target "SRFI-125"
  :std-rejected ("Motoi-own" "sister-dialect-substrate")
  :status "dropped"
  :training-eligible #t
  :provenance "scheme/reference/broken-examples/hash-short-aliases-dropped.slatl"

  ;; ─── THE BROKEN CODE (unbound symbols) ───
  :broken-code "(define h (make-hash-table))\n(hash-set! h 'k 42)\n(display (hash-ref h 'k #f))\n(newline)"
  :broken-output "error: unbound symbol: hash-set!"
  :runs "no — hash-set! and hash-ref are not bound in Motoi's wired surface"

  ;; ─── WHY IT IS BROKEN ───
  :why
"`hash-set!` and `hash-ref` were ergonomic short names carried for source-level
portability with Motoi carts. They are not SRFI-125 names. The locked standard
requires the SRFI-125 spellings, and keeping short aliases would duplicate
standard verbs under divergent names — the exact anti-pattern the conformance
ladder forbids. Both were unbound so there is one wired name per operation.

Note the mixed shape of the old aliases: `hash-ref`'s third argument was a
plain VALUE default (SRFI-69/Racket style), which maps to
`hash-table-ref/default`, NOT to strict `hash-table-ref` (whose third arg is a
failure thunk — see hash-table-ref-value-default.slatl)."

  ;; ─── THE FIX ───
  :fix-code "(define h (make-hash-table))\n(hash-table-set! h 'k 42)\n(display (hash-table-ref/default h 'k #f))\n(newline)"
  :fix-output "42"
  :fix-runs "yes"
  :fix-note
"`hash-set!` -> `hash-table-set!` (identical semantics). `hash-ref h k default`
-> `hash-table-ref/default h k default` (the value-default reading the short
alias used). Do NOT translate `hash-ref` to strict `hash-table-ref` — that would
reintroduce the thunk-vs-value trap."

  ;; ─── THE LESSON ───
  :lesson
"Cross-dialect convenience aliases are a maintenance liability once a standard
is locked. Motoi keeps exactly one name per SRFI-125 operation. When porting
Motoi code, sweep `hash-set!` -> `hash-table-set!` and `hash-ref` ->
`hash-table-ref/default`; do not re-add the aliases. Rosetta (the compat layer)
is the correct home for dialect name-mapping, not the base language."

  ;; ─── THE SAME IDEA IN THREE OTHER LIBRARIES ───
  :three-other-libs (
    (:lib "SRFI-125"
     :status "canonical: hash-table-set! and hash-table-ref/default"
     :code "(hash-table-set! h 'k 42) (hash-table-ref/default h 'k #f)"
     :note "The target names. One spelling each, no short form.")
    (:lib "Racket"
     :status "hash-set! (mutable) and hash-ref exist as the PRIMARY names"
     :code "(hash-set! h 'k 42) (hash-ref h 'k #f)"
     :note "Racket's primary names happen to be the short forms — which is where the sister-dialect aliases came from. Motoi follows SRFI-125, not Racket, so they are non-standard here.")
    (:lib "Clojure"
     :status "assoc / get on persistent maps (functional, not mutating)"
     :code "(get (assoc m :k 42) :k nil)"
     :note "Different data model entirely; included to show ‘short name’ is not a portable concept across the family.")
  )

  :motoi-standard
"Target: SRFI-125 `hash-table-set!` and `hash-table-ref/default`. The short
aliases `hash-set!` / `hash-ref` dropped from the wired surface 2026-07-24;
verbatim original verb blocks archived under
_archive/32-hash-divergent-blocks-20260724/. Dialect name-mapping belongs in
Rosetta, not the base language.")
